{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "memory/a-name-that-reads-like-two-others-ranks-after-both-and-renumbers-neither",
  "title": "A sender whose name reads like two earlier senders' ranks after both, and neither is renumbered",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4",
    "§10.1 step 12"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-6.4-380"
  ],
  "notes": "Three senders, each named by the name its transport stamps: Lan, then ian, then Ian, which reads like Lan (I and l are confusable) and like ian (in case), while Lan and ian read like neither. Ian ranks after both, 2, and the two earlier senders keep their rank, 1, on their later turns too. Python: core/_authors.py AuthorRegister.rank; tests/test_author_register.py::TestAuthorRegister::test_a_name_alike_two_others_ranks_after_both_and_renumbers_neither.",
